  <!--
    PhantomHomeModules : compile and link verification for the PhantomHome product tree.

    THIS IS NOT A SHIPPED PRODUCT BINARY, and it is not a test runner either.
    Measured under task 211: its only entry point is src\Main.cpp, which is a
    googletest runner, and this project links ZERO test cases.  So main() takes its
    own "no tests discovered" branch, prints that, and returns 1.  That is the whole
    observable behaviour of the executable.  It appears in none of the six .wxs files
    and build\installer\staging does not contain it.  The product is hosted by
    ShadowStrikePhantomService.exe, which carries the 22 PhantomHome_KeepAlive_*
    anchors and is what the MSI installs and the SCM starts.

    WHAT IT IS FOR, and why it must not be deleted: it compiles the sources under
    src\Products\Community\PhantomHome plus src\pch.cpp against PhantomCoreLib, so it
    is the only project that proves that product tree compiles and links on its own.
    .github/workflows/coverity-scan.yml builds it as its Phase 3, so Coverity sees
    those product modules through this project; unlisting it silently drops the whole
    PhantomHome product tree out of static analysis.

    Build configuration work that only matters for a SHIPPED binary belongs in
    ShadowStrikePhantomService.vcxproj rather than here.  See tasks 207 and 212.
  -->
